# SceneryStack teaching-shell layout metric

Use this checklist for every SoftButton teaching-shell sim (Ch 12 Our Universe first; reuse for other chapters).

Source of truth: `universe-scenery/src/shared/TeachingShellLayout.ts`.

## Must pass

1. **No top gloss/hairline on dark stages** — `StageBackdrop(..., { gloss: false })`. The white highlight bar reads as a transparent line over titles on cosmic/dark stages.
2. **Reserved title band** — Title + caption own `STAGE_TITLE_BAND` (~58px). Era/status pills go **top-right** or **bottom-left**, never centered over the caption.
3. **Full-bleed letterbox** — Screen background matches the lab/stage (`SCREEN_BACKGROUND`), not light grey side gutters.
4. **Clip the stage** — Scene + labels use `stageClipShape(...)` so orbits, rays, and particles cannot spill past the rounded frame.
5. **Scale diagrams to the stage** — Orbit / diagram radius ≤ `MAX_ORBIT_FRAC × min(sceneW, sceneH)` (default 0.36).
6. **Offline download is discoverable on the catalog** — Simulation cards show “Download offline HTML” when `offlineHtml` is set (blob download). Do not add an in-sim floating download chip. After package changes, rebuild (`npm run build:universe-offline` or the chapter’s `build:*-offline`) so `public/downloads/*` stays in sync.

## Open behavior

Catalog cards still open `sceneryHtml` in a new tab (PhET Color Vision style). Offline download lives on the catalog card (and detail page), not inside the SceneryStack chrome.
